WEBVTT

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.360
They should be nearly there by now.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.160
Thank you so much for doing this.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.620
Don't mention it. It's the least I can do to help.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.840
They're all out cold, huh?

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.460
They were up early this morning, practicing.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.190
The air is so fresh!

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.870
Okay, so where's the stadium?

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.300
We have another road trip
before we get there.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.780
We stay here tonight and check in tomorrow.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.490
<b><b>Girls' Baseball</b></b>

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.490
<b><b>National Tournament Guide</b></b>

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.490
Didn't you read the guide?

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.060
It's finally happening.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.340
Yeah.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.920
There's a barbecue shelter here!

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.630
Yes, the plan is to cook dinner there.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:09.810
Really?!

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.950
We'll be hitting home runs tomorrow!

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.630
We're not here to play around. 
Don't get carried away.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:20.770
Haven't they published
the tournament brackets yet?

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:22.990
They should be announcing them pretty soon...

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.390
Oh! We're playing the first game!

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:33.150
Say what?

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.730
Who are we playing?

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:36.350
I want to see, too!

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.750
Never underestimate
the power of coincidence.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.620
Jinguji-san?

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.590
Seijo High...

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.970
<b>High School Girls' Baseball Tournament</b>

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.970
<b>Game 1</b>

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.970
<b>Satogahama High School</b>

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.970
vs.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.970
<b>Seijo High School</b>

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:36.980
<b>The National Tournament Begins</b>

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.450
Well, best of luck to both teams!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.910
Cheers!

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.940
Cheers!

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:52.500
Ch-Cheers...

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.790
Okay, girls, come and get it!

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.460
Let's eat!

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.330
It's one thing staying in the same place,

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:03.080
but why do we have to 
eat with our opponents?

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.430
My thoughts exactly.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:08.640
A meal like this tastes better
when everyone eats together.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.600
Plus, renting one grill rather
than two saves us money.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.790
You only recently revived
Seijo's baseball team,

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:18.170
so your budget's pretty tight too, right?

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.600
Eat quickly so we can rest up for tomorrow.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.710
Right.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.580
Here you go.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:40.550
<i>Where's Jinguji-san?</i>

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:56.970
For you.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:03.250
Thank you.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:08.550
What a surprise, huh?

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:11.530
I never imagined we'd face
each other in Game 1.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.340
They look like they're having fun.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.590
You should try to have fun, too!

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:28.510
Remember what I told you before?
Our team isn't like yours.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:35.320
The stuff about best friends
and comrades, you mean?

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.930
Seijo's goal is to reclaim
its standing in girls' baseball.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:40.600
Your team doesn't have
that kind of pressure.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.150
You won the Senior Little League nationals,

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:46.690
so you should know by now that
idealistic friendships only hold you back.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:50.830
I hear you.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:03.250
But now, I've started to think there is
more than one way to build a team.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.210
You really are naïve.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.480
Hey!

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:22.820
I'm Makino, from Seijo.

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:26.760
Are you Kawakita-san,
the girl Sayaka's been coaching?

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.320
Y-Yes.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:32.880
How... did that come about, exactly?

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:36.620
Wait, did it cause problems for you?

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.330
N-No, it's not that!

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.500
It's just...

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:45.050
I was surprised to hear
she was doing something like that.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.720
I guess I kind of pushed her into it.

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:56.610
Pushed her into it?

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.770
Okay, lights out.

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:06.300
Goodnight!

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:14.130
I heard the girls who signed
our petition for club status

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:17.490
are gonna be there to cheer us on tomorrow.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.950
My mom contacted me
to say she'll be there, too.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.730
Mine, too.

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.150
My brother said he'd come.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.190
Bathroom...

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.450
Me, too.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:40.150
Me, too.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:42.530
Didn't you just go?

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:46.620
Nozaki-san?

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:51.100
Um... I was thinking of
doing some practice swings...

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:54.030
You're all just nervous.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.170
And you're not, huh?

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:59.750
'Course I am! What do you take me for?!

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.690
I guess it's to be expected.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:04.190
I hope sleep comes soon...

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:09.120
Not right away, probably.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:13.220
Then, I guess now's a good time to
say something I've been meaning to.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.770
Thank you for coming this far with me.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.450
You don't need to thank us.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:41.330
Every one of us is here because we want to be.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:46.540
Yeah. I just didn't want it left unsaid.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:31.460
<i>And those are all the schools
participating in the tournament.</i>

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:44.630
The opening ceremony's already started!

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.050
No complaining!

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:48.250
I did the round trip as fast as I could.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:50.530
Thank you very much, Sensei.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:54.650
Um... Where is...

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:57.240
I think it might be over there.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:00.570
<i>Returning the victor's flag...</i>

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:05.910
<i>...is the captain of last year's 
winning team, Kaio High School:</i>

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.620
<i>Kusakari Rena-san.</i>

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.720
Without further ado...

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:22.270
<i>...the High School Girls' Baseball 
Tournament will now begin.</i>

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:30.480
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:30.480
<b>Seijo</b>

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:30.480
<i>Game 1 is between Satogahama
High School and Seijo High School.</i>

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:32.560
Arihara-san!

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.430
We're here!

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:35.970
You've got this!

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:51.250
To restore our prestige,
victory is the only acceptable outcome.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:53.920
Let's each do our part,

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.610
and bring home the championship.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.620
There are so many people here.

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:02.850
Before I took up baseball, 
all I really did was cheer,

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:04.850
so being down here feels a little weird.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.340
Sounds like everyone's still nervous.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:08.560
You're right.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.360
But now that we've come this far, well...

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:13.020
We just have to do it!

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.360
Yep!

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:15.410
Let's do it!

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:16.690
Yeah!

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:17.900
Assemble!

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.610
Right!

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.810
Let's have a good game!

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.670
<i>Her fastball's looking good.</i>

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.660
<i>Her slider's a bit off.</i>

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:15.080
<i>We should build our
strategy around fastballs.</i>

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:17.040
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:17.040
<b>Seijo</b>

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.670
Well, here I go!

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:24.380
Go get 'em, Vanguard!

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:27.550
Play ball!

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:39.900
Strike!

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:41.860
<i>So fast...</i>

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:53.810
Strike three!

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:00.870
That's not gonna be easy to hit.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.690
Watch me.

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.720
A drag bunt!

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:20.230
Way to go!

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:20.980
Yes!

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:22.190
Sorry!

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:24.980
Don't worry about it.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:30.080
<i>She was wildly unpredictable
in the practice game, too.</i>

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.790
<i>So they have a runner on first...</i>

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:40.950
Play!

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:55.830
Got it!

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:08.850
Nice!

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:09.700
That's it!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.530
Sorry, Jinguji-san.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:13.810
Next time.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:15.110
R-Right...

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:32.950
Strike!

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:37.350
Ball!

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.540
Senpai! Go, go!

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:04.210
Go, go!

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.300
Back to home!

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.900
Asada-senpai!

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:11.470
Go!

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.190
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.190
<b>Seijo</b>

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:34.570
I did it!

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:35.820
Way to go!

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:54.940
Out!

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:57.820
We're doing well!

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:00.060
We can't let our guard down.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:03.750
Jinguji-san is every bit 
as good as Kosaka-san...

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:06.020
One of the best pitchers in the tournament.

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:10.930
We scored the first run last time too,
but they still ended up steamrolling us.

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:13.950
Indeed. We need to stay focused.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:18.010
<i>We worked so hard on our defense,
and it's falling apart at crucial times...</i>

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.710
<i>Everyone's really tense,
since this is our first official game.</i>

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.420
<i>It looks like...</i>

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:28.020
<i>they've improved more than I expected.</i>

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:33.010
I guess it's time.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:48.570
Out!

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:51.030
Nice play!

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:54.990
That feast last night has given me a boost!

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:56.690
You're so cool!

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:58.950
Asada-san's sure playing well.

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:16.930
Out!

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.060
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.060
<b>Seijo</b>

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:32.110
Nozaki-san, you can do it!

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:35.790
Ball!

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:38.990
Ball four!

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.830
Good eye!

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:53.460
Home... run!

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:56.970
Strike! You're out!

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:01.790
<i>That works for Iwaki-senpai.</i>

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:05.020
<i>When she finally hits it, it'll go miles.</i>

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:17.310
<i>Out of everyone on our regular roster,
I'm the weakest, strength-wise.</i>

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:22.290
<i>But I can still support
the others in my own way.</i>

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:26.290
<i>I don't think so!</i>

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:39.770
First!

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:43.810
Safe!

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:45.350
Safe!

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:52.520
Nice bunt!

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:56.030
Suzuki-san?

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:01.870
This is... my first time 
standing on base in a game...

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.130
Way to go.

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:11.540
Sayaka...

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:15.500
I should have thrown it to first base.

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:32.400
Let's continue.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.740
Ball!

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:47.190
Ball four!

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:06.740
She literally slapped some 
focus back into herself.

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:32.040
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:32.040
<b>Seijo</b>

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.670
Let's be more selective over
what pitches we swing at.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.950
<i>We need to watch out for long hits.</i>

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:42.270
Outfield!

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:07.660
<i>It's okay. Just keep calm.</i>

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.380
<i>Down the middle?</i>

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:21.800
Strike!

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:33.520
<i>They're waiting on specific pitches?</i>

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:36.980
<i>Still, if she can keep pitching a good line,</i>

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.030
<i>they'll have trouble getting hits.</i>

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:49.370
Get one first!

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.750
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.750
<b>Seijo</b>

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:56.500
They tied it up already...

00:22:03.410 --> 00:22:04.750
<i>We can't lose...</i>

00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:10.910
<i>Not this early.</i>

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:20.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:20.020
<b>The Hottest Summer Ever</b>
